{"content":"This confirms `startBackgroundRunners` (server.go:153) is the only place background runners get wired up, and it starts exactly one continuous loop: the s3presign runner. `memopayload.Runner` (server/runner/memopayload/runner.go) has no `Run`/ticker loop at all — it's only invoked synchronously via `RebuildMemoPayload` inline in `memo_service.go`, not started as a background worker.\n\nq28.\n\n**Background workers actually started by the server** (wired in `server/server.go:153-174`, `startBackgroundRunners`, called from `Server.Start` at `server/server.go:129`):\n\n- **s3presign runner** (`server/runner/s3presign/runner.go`) — trigger: `time.NewTicker(runnerInterval)` where `runnerInterval = 12h` (`server/runner/s3presign/runner.go:27,30`). It's run once immediately via `RunOnce` at startup (`server/server.go:163`), then launched as a goroutine calling `Run(s3Context)` (`server/server.go:167-171`) which loops on the ticker until its per-runner cancel context fires on shutdown.\n\nThat's the only continuous background runner the server starts. Everything else that looks like a \"worker\" is not an independent scheduled loop:\n\n- `memopayload.Runner` (`server/runner/memopayload/runner.go`) has a `RunOnce` method but no ticker/loop of its own, and it is never instantiated or scheduled anywhere in `server/` or `cmd/` (confirmed no `memopayload.NewRunner` call outside its own package). Its logic (`RebuildMemoPayload`) is invoked synchronously inline from request handling in `server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:108,447` on memo create/update — not a background worker.\n- The SSE heartbeat (`server/router/api/v1/sse_handler.go:64`) is a per-connection ticker inside the request handler, not a server-level background runner.\n- `authenticator.go:180`'s `go func()` is a one-shot fire-and-forget goroutine to record PAT usage, not a scheduled/recurring runner.\n\n**Unused scheduling infrastructure:** `internal/scheduler` — a full custom cron-style scheduler package (`internal/scheduler/scheduler.go`, `parser.go`, with cron-expression parsing and its own README describing it as an alternative to `robfig/cron`/`gocron`) exists in the codebase but is **never imported** by `server/` or `cmd/`. The only references to it are its own README, `doc.go`, `example_test.go`, and `integration_test.go` — it is dead/unused infrastructure, not wired into the running server at all.","iteration":15,"turn":1,"type":"assistant"}
